{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Yet I know that you do not yet fear, and the flax and the barley were struck.</b> The verses are linked: before you fear because of YHWH Elohim, and before you confess and say, ״HaShem is righteous, and I and my people are wicked״ (Exodus 9:27), the flax and the barley had already been struck — for they were ripe and beyond remedy; but the wheat and the spelt, which are food for man, were not yet struck, and that is what remained for you, if you do not continue to sin. Thus explained our master Saadiah Gaon, of blessed memory. <b>And the flax was in stalk.</b> גבעול — that is, the seed had already entered it and grown, therefore it was broken."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:16.982338085Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}